        "client_msg_id": "314e5466-1676-4138-8131-530d69e30fb6",
        "text": "Yay forr hearing San Francisco Public Press mentioned to KQED's \"_*575,233 average weekly radio listeners\"*_\n\nSo glad you <@U07BW27EEHF> mentioned (and they kept in) WHY people are in certain neighborhoods -- history of redlining and legal history and covenants etc determining where BIPOC people were\/are allowed to live.\n\nI say \"ugg\" far as the non-Audrey part of the strange little piece including paraphrasing Wade Crowfoot that \"well intentioned environmental laws are a barrier\" This same ole saw about blaming CEQA :disappointed: and then an Erzra Klein clip from Newsome's podcast saying that CA suffers from \"self-imposed scarcity\" (huh?) and that we need to \"move faster\" ---again code for get CEQA outta the way and build more high priced housing :-} and then paraphrasing Crowfoot again that we need more \"emergency declarations to help skirt normal review.\" _Gunning for CEQA big time._\n\nDid any people you spoke to about long clean up times try to blame CEQA instead of the simple high cost of cleanups?  I suspect the attacks on CEQA will come up if you decide to look at rushing to build upon toxic sites...But you know me.",
